{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/52","id":4686877956,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABF1wVBA","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/52","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/52.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/52.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/52","number":52,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"research(30000644): correct already-solved 2007 reduction-map theorem","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Already solved in the cited original source\n\nThe exact Q-algebra reduction-map surjectivity theorem was proved by Arno van den Essen, Stefan Maubach and Stéphane Vénéreau, JPAA 210 (2007), 141–146, DOI 10.1016/j.jpaa.2006.09.013. The original OWR report p.26 explicitly answers YES immediately after the extracted question; the 2007 Acta problem collection independently confirms every commutative unital ring containing Q and all m,n≥1.\n\nThis is a source-curation correction, with no new discovery claim. Recommended queue status: already_solved, 0/5 new proof-search attempts. The coordinator owns the queue edit.\n\n## Checked proof and scope\n\nThe package gives a fully credited self-contained reconstruction: divergence-free vectors decompose into exact special shears, and finite t-adic corrections lift the prescribed automorphism. Arbitrary nonreduced Q-algebras are included. There is no assumption that a Jacobian-one endomorphism is automatically invertible and no assertion that every base-ring automorphism is tame.\n\nThe full OWR and Acta sources were recovered and their decisive pages visually checked. The full JPAA journal article was not recovered; this access limitation remains explicit. The reconstruction is not described as a line-by-line audit of that unavailable paper.\n\n## Independent review\n\nA separate adversarial review passed the exact source scope and proof, including nonlinear, nilpotent-ring and zero-divisor controls. All 211 author assertions and 142 independent assertions passed. The final header-only proof hash is covered by the review. Actual model: gpt-6-astra, xhigh.\n\nRun `python3 unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30000644/verify.py` with SymPy 1.14.0. The review folder also retains the frozen snapshot needed to replay its copied submitted verifier.\n","created_at":"2026-09-30T06:42:24Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T06:46:21Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"d050cf7d561b640a313c710dff0365764ba3063d","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/52/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/52/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/52/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/statuses/d40d2dae4cff2a5e5a1e